# Target C — cubic curvature windows for individual harmonic components

```text
small attachment diameter -> low-curvature mass on a completion normal interval
-> additive cubic area-deficit charge + dyadic attachment capacity
-> c_I = O(sqrt(D)), and every component
has delta_r + 2 = Omega(D^(1/3)) -> bounded/tree contact cores are excluded.
Still missing: a full-source competitor or exact triangle for the surviving
large components and contact-isolated population. This chain does not close C-II.
```

